# trivy vulnerability ignore list for this repo (auto-loaded by trivy from CWD).
# Accepted-risk findings that cannot be fixed at this layer — mirror .grype.yaml.

# bleve query-string DoS. bleve v1.0.14 is a TRANSITIVE dependency of git-bug
# (kref/internal/entry -> git-bug/repository -> bleve); no fixed v1 release exists
# and v2 is a breaking module-path change, so kref cannot upgrade it on its own.
# Revisit when git-bug moves to a patched bleve.
CVE-2022-31022

# golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp is unmaintained and unsafe by design. The advisory
# is scoped to that ONE package, but trivy and grype match at module granularity,
# so they flag golang.org/x/crypto as a whole. kref never reaches the package:
# `go mod why golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp` reports "main module does not need"
# it, and the build graph pulls github.com/ProtonMail/go-crypto/openpgp — the
# maintained fork the advisory itself recommends. govulncheck (symbol-level
# reachability, security.yml) agrees and reports nothing. There is no fixed
# version because the package will never be fixed, only removed; re-check if a
# dependency ever imports it for real.
GO-2026-5932
